  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CoCreate Circular Textiles</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bangladesh&apos; main industry is the production of Ready Made Garments (RMG), which currently generates around 600,000 metric tons of textile and garment waste every year. Part of this is being used to produce children&apos;s clothing, or in the bedding sector (mattresses, pillows, cushions, seat padding, etc) or shipped abroad.With the new procurement rules of the EU, it is vital for large Dutch textile purchasers that production processes are green and circular. A shift from linear to circular fashion in Bangladesh will potentially create an additional economy of US$5 billion, save 840 million m3 of water, 3 million tons of CO2 equivalent and create a new hub of employment.In response  to these RMG waste challenges, this project engages Bangladeshi students in two three-month hackathons to address real-life issues faced by local private sector players. Insights gained will be turned into educational materials for integration into Bangladeshi curricula.The programme aims to instill design thinking and market-oriented learning, fostering collaboration among stakeholders and cultivating a critical mindset in young minds for future circular textile practices and innovations.</narrative>
  </description>
